# Brenz language and naming

## Rules
- Write documentation, rules, decisions, comments, commit messages, file names and folder names in English.
- Write types, functions, variables, enums, tokens, Firestore fields and String Catalog keys in English.
- Keep user-facing Spanish only in `Localizable.xcstrings` (`es`). English is the base (`en`).
- Name the same concept with the same word everywhere. Do not mix synonyms.
- Use the glossary below for product terms.
- Write quoted UI copy in a doc as the `es` string and mark it `(es)`.
- Name files `brenz-<topic>.md`, `brenz-architecture-<layer>.md` and `brenz-rule-<topic>.mdc`.

## Glossary (product term → code term)
- class (training session) → `class` in prose, `ClassLog` in code
- glass of water → `WaterLog`
- character → `Character`; pet state → `PetState`
- states: animado → `animated`, normal → `normal`, decaído → `down`, flojera → `lazy`
- stage → `Stage` (key 1, 2, 3). Names live in the catalog (`stage.1.name`).
- board → `DayBoard`; tile → tile; slab → slab; row → row; cell → cell
- bubble → speech bubble
- Home tab "Entrena" → Train; "Historial" → History; "Ajustes" → Settings
- Inicio → Start; Introducción → Intro; Crear cuenta → Sign Up; Iniciar sesión → Sign In; Recuperar contraseña → Reset Password; Cambiar contraseña → Change Password; Borrar cuenta → Delete Account; Cerrar sesión → Sign Out
- Colors: fondo → `background`; superficie → `surface`; superficieAlta → `surfaceHigh`; acento → `accent`; agua → `water`; texto → `textPrimary`; textoSecundario → `textSecondary`; borde → `border`; tarjetaPersonaje → `characterCard`; peligro → `danger`; línea → `line` (art only)

## Forbidden
- Do not use Spanish or mixed-language identifiers (`registrarClase`, `claseLog`, `fondoColor`).
- Do not write Spanish in code comments, commit messages or documentation.
- Do not name files with Spanish words.
- Do not hardcode visible text in code, in either language.
